# Modular Architecture Rules (STRICT)
You MUST follow this architecture when generating code.
## Module Structure
- All business logic MUST be inside src/main/modules/
- Each module MUST contain:
  - *.repo.ts (database access only)
  - *.handler.ts (IPC handler only)
- Modules MUST be auto-loaded by a module loader
- NEVER manually import modules in main index
## Separation Rules
- Repositories:
  - MUST contain only database logic (CRUD)
  - MUST NOT contain IPC or UI logic
- Handlers:
  - MUST call repositories
  - MUST NOT contain raw SQL
## IPC Rules
- All IPC channels MUST follow:
  format: module:action
Examples:
- project:create
- task:update
- Renderer MUST NOT define its own API names
- Renderer MUST use generic invoke:
  window.api.invoke(channel, data)
## Renderer Rules
- Renderer MUST NOT directly call specific functions like:
  ❌ createProject()
  ❌ getTasks()
- ALWAYS use:
  window.api.invoke("module:action", data)
## Dependency Rules
- Modules MUST NOT import other modules directly
- Shared logic MUST go into shared/
## Enforcement
If any code violates these rules:
- You MUST refactor it to follow the architecture
## Module Interface Rules  
Each module MUST export a register(ipcMain) function.  
Example:  
export function register(ipcMain) {  
ipcMain.handle("module:action", async () => {  
...  
})  
}
